        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "b5ac0ffe-6f86-5543-9c52-2e97670859cd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Morgan Paull, Hampton Fancher, David Peoples, Philip K. Dick\n- Works: Blade Runner, Do Androids Dream of Electric Sheep?, Dirty O'Neil\n- Roles: Dave Holden, Jimmy O'Neil\n\nFacts:\n- Philip K. Dick wrote the 1968 novel \"Do Androids Dream of Electric Sheep?\".\n- \"Blade Runner\" was scripted by Hampton Fancher and David Peoples as a loose adaptation of Philip K. Dick's novel \"Do Androids Dream of Electric Sheep?\".\n- Morgan Paull was an American actor born on December 15, 1944, and he was most notable for playing Dave Holden in Ridley Scott's film \"Blade Runner\".\n- In \"Dirty O'Neil,\" Morgan Paull played Jimmy O'Neil, a cop in a small Texas town who is forced into action when three homicidal thugs invade the town.",
